", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I'm starting school soon. vs. I'm going to start school next Monday.<br>  I intend to start school next week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " <br>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> to talk about arrangements and plans. <span class=\"strong\">Be going to</span> puts an emphasis on the idea of intention (decide to do something).<br>   <br>You can use <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">intend to</span></span> in place of be going to.<br> ", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "stomach ache", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pain in a person's stomach ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have a stomach ache from the street food I ate.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le03ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about travel.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "headache ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pain in someone's head ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The hot sun is giving me a headache.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le03ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "open-air", "type": "name"}, {"content": "located outside ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are going to an open-air market.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le03ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "market", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a place where products are bought and sold", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The markets are filled with food!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le03ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "